  <section id="chto-eto">
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>Guyon canal is a small tunnel at the base of the palm on the little-finger side, between the pisiform bone and the hook of the hamate. The ulnar nerve and artery pass through it into the hand. The canal is narrow, so little pressure from outside or inside is enough to trap the nerve.</p>
    <NerveMap limb="arm" focus="guyon" lang="en" />
    <h3>Causes</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>a wrist ganglion cyst — one of the most common causes;</li>
      <li>long pressure on the palm: bicycle handlebars, tools, a cane, crutches;</li>
      <li>wrist fractures and bruises, especially fracture of the hook of the hamate;</li>
      <li>arterial changes, rheumatoid arthritis, rarely tumours.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="simptomy">
    <h2>Symptoms</h2>
    <p>They depend on which part of the nerve is compressed:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>numbness and tingling of the little finger and half of the ring finger on the palm side;</li>
      <li>weakness of small hand muscles: hard to spread and bring fingers together, clumsiness in fine tasks;</li>
      <li>wasting of the muscles between the fingers;</li>
      <li>sometimes — weakness only, without numbness.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="diagnostika">
    <h2>Diagnosis</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Nerve conduction study</strong> — shows that the nerve is affected at the wrist, not at the elbow or in the neck.</li>
      <li><strong>Wrist ultrasound</strong> — finds cysts and nerve swelling.</li>
      <li><strong>Wrist MRI or CT</strong> — if a fracture or a mass is suspected.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="lechenie">
    <h2>Treatment</h2>
    <p><strong>Without surgery</strong> — if the cause is load: remove pressure on the palm, padded gloves and a proper riding position for cyclists, a temporary splint, avoiding the provoking work. Medication is prescribed by a doctor. Five <a href="/en/treatment/nerves/carpal-tunnel-syndrome/#uprazhneniya">hand exercises</a> are in the carpal tunnel article.</p>
    <p><strong>Surgery</strong> — if a cyst or another mass is compressing the nerve, there is muscle weakness, or non-surgical treatment does not help. Through an incision on the palm at the base of the little finger the canal is opened, the cyst removed and the nerve freed. Usually under local anaesthesia.</p>
    <p>After surgery stitches are removed on day 10–14. Sensation and strength return gradually.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="srochno" slot="urgent">
    <h2>When to seek urgent help</h2>
    <div class="callout alert">
      <p>Loss of sensation or finger movement after a wrist injury or cut — <strong>go to an emergency department the same day</strong>. Sudden weakness of the arm and leg on one side, speech problems — <strong>call emergency services immediately (112; 103 in Russia).</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>
